xnu 0290: the small-core scheduler is opt-in and says what it saw

`small_cores` defaulted to 2, so every boot entered the scheduler experiment
and a boot that only wanted the UI could not stay out of it. The default is 0
(no pairing) and the levels are explicit: 2 pairs the cores, 3 lets the
scheduler move threads to a faster core when it frees, 4 adds the running-
thread kick.

The boot prints one line with the topology the device tree gave - the
capacity of every CPU, which ones are small, and the partner each was paired
with - because arm_init runs too early to print and a wrong pairing is
otherwise invisible.

